          "quantifier": "fixed"
        }
      ],
      "quantifier_scope": "For every eps > 0, the tail P(|hat{theta}_n - theta_0| > eps) tends to 0 as n -> infinity, with the estimator built from the maximum over the growing range 1 <= j <= m_n.",
      "probability_model": "The single probability space of Lemma 1 carries the array {X_{n,j}} and hence hat{theta}_n; convergence in probability uses its measure P.",
      "hypotheses": [
        "The conditions of Lemma 1 hold: for each fixed j, X_{n,j} -> 0 in probability, and m_n -> infinity.",
        "hat{theta}_n = theta_0 + max_{1 <= j <= m_n} |X_{n,j}|."
      ],
      "definitions": [
        "Convergence in probability: hat{theta}_n -> theta_0 iff for every eps > 0, P(|hat{theta}_n - theta_0| > eps) -> 0."
      ],
      "conclusion": "hat{theta}_n -> theta_0 in probability as n -> infinity.",
